run-hw.sh: REFUSED -- could not collect from C:\DOSAGS after 1961s (--timeout=1800s).
  get-file's own reboot never completed. Most likely explanation for a slow arm: the game is
  still running. Any running SDL3-DOS game replaces the BIOS keyboard IRQ handler (see the
  comment above this block), so a reboot chord genuinely cannot succeed while it is still
  alive, healthy or not -- this is NOT by itself evidence of a wedge. Re-run with a longer
  --timeout first; only suspect a genuine wedge (docs/lab/OPEN-FAULTS.md sec. 23) after
  ruling that out.
